   "title": "Akwa Ibom Raises Bursary To ₦200,000, Offers Medical, Law Students ₦250,000",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/akwa-ibom-raises-bursary-to-%e2%82%a6200000-offers-medical-law-students-%e2%82%a6250000/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:33:53 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793306033.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "The governor announced the increase during an interactive session on the second day of the Ibom Ignite Conference 2026 in Uyo, the state capital. He said the increase was intended to ease the financial burden on students and their parents, particularly amid rising costs of accommodation, learning materials and other academic needs.",
   "summary_zh": "州长在乌约州首府举行的2026年Ibom Ignite Conference第二天的一场互动活动中宣布了这一增幅。他说，提高收费旨在减轻学生及其父母的经济负担，尤其是在住宿、学习材料和其他学业相关开支不断上涨的情况下。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The governor announced the increase during an interactive session on the second day of the Ibom Ignite Conference 2026 in Uyo, the state capital. He said the increase was intended to ease the financial burden on students and their parents, particularly amid rising costs of accommodation, learning materials and other academic needs. Eno said the initiative underscored the state government’s commitment to education and human capital development by supporting young people with the knowledge, skills and resources needed to succeed. The governor also reaffirmed his administration’s commitment to youth empowerment through skills acquisition, digital training, entrepreneurship development and employment opportunities. He said the government was committed to providing young people with the support, guidance and exposure needed to grow their businesses, realise their potential and contribute to the state’s development. According to him, the administration’s youth empowerment initiatives go beyond providing start-up funds to young entrepreneurs, as beneficiaries are also monitored, mentored and guided to improve their chances of success. Eno further disclosed that trainees at the Youth Development Centre in Oron were nearing graduation, with hundreds of beneficiaries earning certifications from Microsoft and Google. He added that some trainees had acquired coding and other digital skills, creating opportunities for remote employment. “Hundreds of young people in Oron have earned Microsoft and Google certifications, with some acquiring coding skills and securing remote job opportunities. We will extend the programme to other locations,” the governor stated. Delivering a keynote address titled “Building Beyond Boundaries,” the Chief Executive Officer of Hensek Integrated Limited, Engr. Uwem Okoko, highlighted the importance of vision, innovation and determination in driving development beyond conventional limits. He urged individuals and organisations to look beyond existing limitations, embrace new possibilities and remain committed to turning their aspirations into reality. Similarly, Dr. Maxwell Ubah of Strategy House Limited, in a presentation titled “Change Your Thinking, Change Your Future,” challenged participants to cultivate a positive mindset, reinvent themselves and remain focused on their goals. Ubah encouraged participants to approach their personal and professional pursuits with the right attitude, discipline and dedication, noting that a change in mindset could help unlock their potential and position them for greater success. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
