   "title": "Korea to conditionally ease diesel export restrictions amid stable crude supplies",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/business/20261029/korea-to-conditionally-ease-diesel-export-restrictions-amid-stable-crude-supplies",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:42:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793241723.0,
   "ageDays": 0.76,
   "summary": "Korea will ease export restrictions currently imposed on diesel starting in November on condition that domestic supply remains stable, the industry ministry said Thursday. Korea adopted export restrictions on fuel products when it implemented the oil price cap system in March to maintain stable domestic supply. The industry ministry said crude supplies remain stable, citing crude import volumes for October and November equivalent to at least 100 percent of last year's monthly average.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国产业通商部周四表示，只要国内供应保持稳定，韩国将从11月起放宽目前对柴油实施的出口限制。韩国于3月实施油价上限制度时，对燃料产品采取出口限制，以维持国内供应稳定。产业通商部援引10月和11月原油进口量称，原油供应保持稳定，两个月的进口量均相当于去年同期月均进口量的至少100%。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea will ease export restrictions currently imposed on diesel starting in November on condition that domestic supply remains stable, the industry ministry said Thursday. The Ministry of Trade, Industry and Resources said the government will allow diesel exports of up to 110 percent of the volume recorded in the same month a year earlier, up from the current cap of 100 percent. The higher cap will apply only when oil refiners fulfill their domestic supply obligations and maintain adequate inventories, the ministry added. Korea adopted export restrictions on fuel products when it implemented the oil price cap system in March to maintain stable domestic supply. Local oil refiners have recently called for such restrictions to be eased. The industry ministry said crude supplies remain stable, citing crude import volumes for October and November equivalent to at least 100 percent of last year's monthly average. \"With tensions in the Middle East lingering, the government will closely monitor the supply of petroleum products and immediately reinstate the previous cap should further supply concerns arise,\" a ministry official said",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
