   "title": "In a first since 2023, Delhi invites Pakistan Minister for inaugural SCO Civilisational Dialogue in November",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/in-a-first-since-2023-delhi-invites-pakistan-minister-for-inaugural-sco-civilisational-dialogue-in-november/article71630539.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:15:39 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793159139.0,
   "ageDays": 1.71,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription India will hold the first “ Civilisational Dialogue Forum ” of the 10-nation Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) grouping, that includes Pakistan, from November 20-22 in Delhi, sources confirmed to The Hindu . The dialogue, which will be organised by the Ministry of Culture and the Ministry of External Affairs, was proposed by Prime Minister Narendra Modi at the SCO leaders’ Summit in Tianjin last year and adopted by the SCO Council.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁：消息人士向《The Hindu》证实，包括巴基斯坦在内的10国上海合作组织（SCO）将于11月20日至22日在德里举行首届“文明对话论坛”。这场对话由文化和外交部门组织，最初由总理纳伦德拉·莫迪去年在天津举行的SCO领导人峰会上提出，并获SCO理事会通过。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription India will hold the first “ Civilisational Dialogue Forum ” of the 10-nation Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) grouping, that includes Pakistan, from November 20-22 in Delhi, sources confirmed to The Hindu . The dialogue, which will be organised by the Ministry of Culture and the Ministry of External Affairs, was proposed by Prime Minister Narendra Modi at the SCO leaders’ Summit in Tianjin last year and adopted by the SCO Council. According to the sources, the government has invited Pakistan’s Minister for National Heritage and Culture Aurungzeb Khan Khichi, for the event. Culture Ministers from the 10 member states, including China, Russia, Iran, Belarus and Central Asian states, 15 Dialogue partners and observer countries have been invited. The event, which will be inaugurated by Mr. Modi, will be held at Delhi’s iconic Purana Quila (Old Fort), a 16th Century fort built by Emperor Humayun. The fort is also the site of many excavations showcasing India’s ancient past spanning nearly 3,000 years, from the Pre-Mauryan, Mauryan, Sunga, Kushana, Gupta, Post-Gupta period to medieval-era Rajput, Sultanate and Mughal periods, officials said, explaining its importance. According to diplomatic sources, Pakistan has not so far confirmed who will lead its delegation to the dialogue forum. If Mr. Khichi attends, this will be the first time India will host a Minister from Pakistan since the 2023 SCO Foreign Ministers meeting, when the then Pakistan FM Bilawal Bhutto had travelled to Goa , and the first since the four-day conflict between India and Pakistan in May 2025. While the Modi government has refused to take part in meetings of South Asia Association for Regional Cooperation (SAARC) in Islamabad due to differences with Pakistan since 2016, it has joined SCO meetings there in the past, including SCO-Regional Anti-Terror Structure (RATS). In September, India sent SCO National Coordinator Alok Dimri to Islamabad to attend the first coordination meeting for Pakistan’s SCO Presidency and events leading up to the leader’s Summit in Pakistan, scheduled for August 2027. In November 2024, External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar had represented India at the SCO Heads of Government (HoG) Meeting , and all eyes will be in who will represent India at the SCO Heads of State Summit next year. Also Read | At SCO meet, Rajnath calls for dismantling the entire ecosystem of terrorism “India deals with SCO as an entity, as an important organisation,” MEA Secretary (West) Sibi George said in response to a question from The Hindu at a briefing on August 27 about whether PM Modi would travel to Pakistan for the summit. “As far as our engagement with individual countries is concerned, a decision will be taken by the appropriate authority at the appropriate time and our appropriate level of participation will be decided accordingly”, he added. international relations / diplomacy / summit / Pakistan / India-Pakistan Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ru",
    "in"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
