   "title": "Hanwha Defense USA to take control of Philly Shipyard in internal restructuring",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/world/20261028/hanwha-defense-usa-to-take-control-of-philly-shipyard-in-internal-restructuring",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:37:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793155022.0,
   "ageDays": 1.76,
   "summary": "WASHINGTON — Hanwha Defense USA (HDUSA) said Tuesday it will acquire a controlling stake in Hanwha Philly Shipyard, part of a broader internal restructuring aimed at strengthening the South Korean conglomerate's U.S. naval shipbuilding operations. Under a restructuring plan announced in September, Hanwha Systems Co. will sell its 60 percent stake in the shipyard to Hanwha Defense USA Shipbuilding LLC, a joint venture involving HDUSA and Hanwha FutureProof.",
   "summary_zh": "华盛顿——韩华防务美国公司（HDUSA）周二表示，将收购韩华费城造船厂的控股权。这是韩国大型综合企业集团为加强其美国海军造船业务而进行的更广泛内部重组的一部分。根据9月公布的重组计划，韩华系统株式会社将把其在该造船厂持有的60%股份出售给韩华防务美国造船有限责任公司。后者是由HDUSA与韩华FutureProof组成的合资企业。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "WASHINGTON — Hanwha Defense USA (HDUSA) said Tuesday it will acquire a controlling stake in Hanwha Philly Shipyard, part of a broader internal restructuring aimed at strengthening the South Korean conglomerate's U.S. naval shipbuilding operations. Under a restructuring plan announced in September, Hanwha Systems Co. will sell its 60 percent stake in the shipyard to Hanwha Defense USA Shipbuilding LLC, a joint venture involving HDUSA and Hanwha FutureProof. Hanwha Ocean Co. will retain its 40 percent stake. HDUSA said the move will bring the Philadelphia-based shipyard under its leadership as Hanwha seeks to transform the facility into a dual-use shipyard capable of building vessels for the U.S. Navy and commercial customers. \"As HDUSA continues to grow its multi-domain presence across the U.S., bringing the Philly Shipyard under HDUSA will further align our government and commercial shipbuilding efforts,\" HDUSA President and Chief Executive Officer (CEO) Michael Coulter said in a statement. Retired U.S. Navy Rear Adm. Tom Anderson, president of U.S. shipbuilding at HDUSA, will oversee the company's American shipbuilding operations as it prepares the facility to serve military and commercial customers. South Korea's Hanwha Group acquired the Philadelphia shipyard in December 2024 as part of its push into the U.S. shipbuilding market, with the latest restructuring aimed at consolidating its defense and shipbuilding capabilities in the country",
