   "title": "Bandits Storm Kaduna Millennium City Again, Abduct 6 Residents",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/bandits-storm-kaduna-millennium-city-again-abduct-6-residents/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:36:55 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793155015.0,
   "ageDays": 1.76,
   "summary": "Millennium City, a fast-growing Kaduna suburb, has survived several kidnapping incidents, with locals expressing worries over the inability of both the federal and the state government to bring the lingering security situation under control. Millennium City was also the scene of the October 6 abduction of Ahmed Abubakar Zakka, his wife and their six-month-old daughter, Fatima, from Alrahus Estate.",
   "summary_zh": "快速发展的卡杜纳郊区Millennium City曾经历多起绑架事件，当地居民对联邦政府和州政府均无法控制持续的安全局势表示担忧。Millennium City也是10月6日Ahmed Abubakar Zakka、其妻子以及他们六个月大的女儿Fatima从Alrahus Estate遭绑架的地点。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Available information showed that early military personnel intervention led to the rescue of some of the victims. Millennium City, a fast-growing Kaduna suburb, has survived several kidnapping incidents, with locals expressing worries over the inability of both the federal and the state government to bring the lingering security situation under control. Millennium City was also the scene of the October 6 abduction of Ahmed Abubakar Zakka, his wife and their six-month-old daughter, Fatima, from Alrahus Estate. A resident, who identified herself as Maman Hamid and lives close to the victims’ houses, revealed that the attackers gained access to the estate through its second gate before carrying out the operation. Hamid said the incident threw residents into panic, adding that military personnel pursued the suspected kidnappers and rescued some of the victims, although the assailants escaped. The number of people rescued and the whereabouts of those still missing were not immediately established as of the time of filing this report. The latest attack comes less than two weeks after police authorities reportedly announced the arrest of eight suspected kidnappers and four alleged informants during operations around Millennium City and Maraban Rido on October 12, with AK-47 rifles recovered. As of the time of filing this report, neither the Kaduna State Police Command nor the Ministry for Internal Security and Home Affairs have made public statements on the development. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
