   "_dt": 1793133063.0,
   "ageDays": 2.02,
   "summary": "The Federal Government has approved a N70,000 monthly transport intervention for public service workers across all levels for six months, beginning in November 2026, to cushion the impact of rising living costs. The approval was one of the resolutions reached at a conciliation meeting between the Federal Government and the leadership of the Nigeria Labour Congress (NLC) in Abuja on Tuesday, following renewed pressure from organised labour over the rising cost of living, workers’ welfare and outstanding agreements.",
   "summary_zh": "联邦政府已批准从2026年11月起，连续6个月向各级公共服务人员每月发放7万奈拉交通补贴，以缓解生活成本上涨带来的影响。这是联邦政府与尼日利亚劳工大会（NLC）领导层周二在阿布贾召开调解会议后达成的决议之一。此前，有组织劳工因生活成本上涨、工人福利及尚未履行的协议而再次向政府施压。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Federal Government has approved a N70,000 monthly transport intervention for public service workers across all levels for six months, beginning in November 2026, to cushion the impact of rising living costs. The approval was one of the resolutions reached at a conciliation meeting between the Federal Government and the leadership of the Nigeria Labour Congress (NLC) in Abuja on Tuesday, following renewed pressure from organised labour over the rising cost of living, workers’ welfare and outstanding agreements. The government also approved the payment of peculiar allowance arrears, effective from May 1, 2026, in three equal monthly instalments beginning in November. However, the meeting ended without an agreement on the effective date for implementing the national minimum wage. Both parties agreed that the Minimum Wage Negotiation Committee would be constituted and commence meetings immediately to address the outstanding issue. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
