   "title": "Reps Demand Regulation Of Electric, CNG Vehicles Importation",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/reps-demand-regulation-of-electric-cng-vehicles-importation/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:59:12 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793120352.0,
   "ageDays": 2.16,
   "summary": "Consequently, the House urged the Federal Government to establish a transparent licensing and approval framework for the commercial importation of EVs, CNG vehicles and related clean mobility equipment. Moving the motion, he noted that Nigeria had adopted policies promoting the transition to EVs, CNG vehicles, Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) vehicles, and other clean transportation technologies as part of its energy transition and economic diversification agenda.",
   "summary_zh": "因此，众议院敦促联邦政府为电动汽车、压缩天然气汽车及相关清洁出行设备的商业进口建立透明的许可和审批框架。提出该动议时，他指出，作为尼日利亚能源转型和经济多元化议程的一部分，尼日利亚已经采取了促进向电动汽车、压缩天然气汽车、液化石油气汽车及其他清洁交通技术转型的政策。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Consequently, the House urged the Federal Government to establish a transparent licensing and approval framework for the commercial importation of EVs, CNG vehicles and related clean mobility equipment. It asked the National Automotive Design and Development Council (NADDC), in collaboration with the Bureau of Public Procurement (BPP), the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), the Nigeria Customs Service (NCS), and other relevant agencies, to develop objective qualification criteria for import approval. These resolutions were a result of the adoption of a motion sponsored by Hon. Ademorin Aliu Kuye(APC, Lagos) at plenary on Tuesday. Moving the motion, he noted that Nigeria had adopted policies promoting the transition to EVs, CNG vehicles, Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) vehicles, and other clean transportation technologies as part of its energy transition and economic diversification agenda. According to him, Nigeria has the opportunity to encourage local investment, technology transfer, employment generation, and domestic value addition by linking import incentives to measurable investments in infrastructure and technical capacity. It further asked the Federal Government to align tax incentives, import duty concessions, and other fiscal benefits with compliance with this regulatory framework to promote sustained investment in local infrastructure. The House mandated the Committees on Industry, Commerce, Gas Resources, Environment, and Legislative Compliance to monitor implementation and report within four weeks for legislative action. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "eco",
    "ene"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_leadership",
   "title_zh": "议员要求监管电动车和压缩天然气汽车进口",
   "body_zh": "因此，议院敦促联邦政府为电动汽车、压缩天然气汽车及相关清洁出行设备的商业进口建立透明的许可与审批框架。议院要求国家汽车设计与开发委员会（NADDC）与公共采购局（BPP）、尼日利亚标准组织（SON）、尼日利亚海关总署（NCS）及其他相关机构合作，制定客观的进口审批资格标准。这些决议源于周二的全体会议上通过了一项由尊敬的 Ademorin Aliu Kuye（APC，拉各斯州）提出的动议。提出该动议时，他指出，作为能源转型和经济多元化议程的一部分，尼日利亚已经出台政策，推动向电动汽车、压缩天然气汽车、液化石油气（LPG）汽车及其他清洁交通技术过渡。据他表示，尼日利亚可以把握机遇，将进口激励措施与对基础设施和技术能力的可量化投资相挂钩，从而促进本地投资、技术转让、创造就业机会和提升国内附加值。决议还要求联邦政府使税收优惠、进口关税减让及其他财政利益与遵守该监管框架的要求相协调，以推动对本地基础设施的持续投资。议院责成工业、商业、天然气资源、环境和立法合规委员会监督执行情况，并在四周内提交报告，以便采取立法行动。我们掌握最新动态。获取实时报道、突发独家内幕和独家视角，直接推送到您的手机。不要满足于陈旧新闻。加入 LEADERSHIP NEWS WhatsApp 频道，随时随地接收 24/7 更新 →",
