   "title": "Mercedes-Benz cuts 2026 profit outlook on tough China market",
   "url": "https://punchng.com/mercedes-benz-cuts-2026-profit-outlook-on-tough-china-market/",
   "domain": "punchng.com",
   "source": "Punch（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:19:39 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793103579.0,
   "ageDays": 2.36,
   "summary": "German premium carmaker Mercedes-Benz on Tuesday cut its outlook for the year, citing tough conditions in China and higher material costs. The news makes Mercedes the last of the big three German carmakers to lower their annual outlook after BMW and Volkswagen, both also citing weakness in China, the world’s largest car market. Mercedes-Benz’s vehicle deliveries in China — last year already at their lowest level since 2016 — fell a further 29 percent in the nine months to end-September.",
   "summary_zh": "德国豪华汽车制造商Mercedes-Benz于周二下调了本年度业绩展望，理由是中国市场环境严峻及原材料成本上升。至此，在BMW和Volkswagen之后，Mercedes-Benz成为最后一家下调年度展望的德国三大汽车制造商；这两家公司也都提到了全球最大汽车市场中国的疲软。Mercedes-Benz在中国的汽车交付量继去年降至2016年以来最低水平后，在截至9月底的9个月里又下降了29%。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "German premium carmaker Mercedes-Benz on Tuesday cut its outlook for the year, citing tough conditions in China and higher material costs. Core profit for 2026 is now expected to be on a par with the prior year’s 5.8 billion euros ($6.5 billion), the company said, down from a previously guided increase of at least 15 percent. Profit margins at the core car business are now seen at between two and three percent for the year, the firm said, down from the three to five percent previously expected. The news makes Mercedes the last of the big three German carmakers to lower their annual outlook after BMW and Volkswagen, both also citing weakness in China, the world’s largest car market. Mercedes-Benz’s vehicle deliveries in China — last year already at their lowest level since 2016 — fell a further 29 percent in the nine months to end-September. Local rivals such as Xiaomi and BYD have eaten into market share at the same time as a sluggish domestic economy has weighed on demand",
