   "snippet": "A video circulating on social media has sparked discussion over border security along the India-China frontier. The footage is being shared with claims that Indian Army personnel confronted Chinese People’s Liberation Army (PLA) soldiers allegedly attempting to cross into Indian territory near Arunachal Pradesh.\n\nAccording to the claims accompanying the video, the Chinese personnel were intercepted and later released under established border protocols along the Line of Actual Control (LAC).\n\nHowever, the video’s authenticity, date, location and the circumstances of the alleged confrontation have not been independently verified. No definitive conclusion can be drawn from the circulating footage alone.\n\nIndia and China have experienced border tensions in the past, making incidents along the LAC a matter of significant public interest. The latest claims require confirmation from official sources before the video can be treated as evidence of an actual border confrontation.\n\nFact Check: The specific incident remains unverified. The video’s original source, date and location, along with any official statements from Indian authorities, need to be established. #IndianArmy",
   "body": "A video circulating on social media has sparked discussion over border security along the India-China frontier. The footage is being shared with claims that Indian Army personnel confronted Chinese People’s Liberation Army (PLA) soldiers allegedly attempting to cross into Indian territory near Arunachal Pradesh.\n\nAccording to the claims accompanying the video, the Chinese personnel were intercepted and later released under established border protocols along the Line of Actual Control (LAC).\n\nHowever, the video’s authenticity, date, location and the circumstances of the alleged confrontation have not been independently verified. No definitive conclusion can be drawn from the circulating footage alone.\n\nIndia and China have experienced border tensions in the past, making incidents along the LAC a matter of significant public interest. The latest claims require confirmation from official sources before the video can be treated as evidence of an actual border confrontation.\n\nFact Check: The specific incident remains unverified. The video’s original source, date and location, along with any official statements from Indian authorities, need to be established. #IndianArmy",
